    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II</a> in 1130, it joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in one of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>’s most centralised states.</li><li>Its Norman court mixed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, Greek and Arabic government and art, seen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cefalu-cathedral">Cefalù</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monreale-cathedral">Monreale</a>.</li><li>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-vespers">Vespers</a> of 1282 it survived as an island kingdom under Aragon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and others until 1816.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>From 1530 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a> as a fief of the kingdom, paying the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> an annual tribute of a single falcon.</p></aside>
    </section>

